    "description": "Situated in San Francisco\u2019s highly desirable North of Panhandle (NoPa) neighborhood, 833\u2013837 Scott Street presents a rare opportunity to acquire a low-density, fully occupied multifamily property in a prime central location. Built in 1905, this well-maintained three-unit building features classic Edwardian charm with large bay windows, high ceilings, and intricate period details. The oversized full-floor flats are ideally suited for co-living arrangements, student housing, or large households seeking space and convenience in a walkable urban setting. The large bedroom counts, combined with expansive common areas, provide tenants with flexible and functional layouts that support both privacy and shared living. In addition, each unit benefits from excellent natural light and classic architectural finishes that add long-term value and rental appeal. The building offers an impressive unit mix comprising a 4-bedroom/1.5-bath flat, a 5-bedroom/1.5-bath flat, and a 6-bedroom/2.5-bath flat with washer/dryer which occupies the entire top two floors. There is an additional washer/dryer on the third-floor landing utilized by the bottom two units.  The building floorplans and configurations offer generous living space not commonly available in the San Francisco rental market."
  },
